1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,079
Hi.

2
00:00:02,079 --> 00:00:03,250
Great to see you!

3
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:03,945
I'm Jody,

4
00:00:03,945 --> 00:00:08,812
and I'll be looking after both of you for the first month you've working

5
00:00:08,812 --> 00:00:10,550
here at the Amersham Theatre.

6
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:15,520
I'll tell you something about the theatre now, then take you to meet two

7
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:16,940
of the other staff.

8
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:19,144
It's an old building,

9
00:00:19,144 --> 00:00:22,450
and it's been modernised several times.

10
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:28,050
In fact, as you can see, we're carrying out a major refurbishment at the

11
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:28,450
moment.

12
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:30,868
The interior has just been repainted,

13
00:00:30,868 --> 00:00:35,300
and we're about to start on the exterior of the building

14
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:37,130
that'll be a big job.

15
00:00:37,130 --> 00:00:39,430
The work's running over budget,

16
00:00:39,430 --> 00:00:43,110
so we've had to postpone installing an elevator.

17
00:00:43,110 --> 00:00:46,420
I hope you're happy running up and down stairs!

18
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:52,500
When the theatre was built, people were generally slimmer and shorter than now,

19
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:55,030
and the seats were very close together.

20
00:00:55,030 --> 00:00:59,500
We've replaced them with larger seats, with more legroom.

21
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:05,616
This means fewer seats in total but we've taken the opportunity to install seats

22
00:01:05,616 --> 00:01:07,800
that can easily be moved,

23
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:10,000
to create different acting spaces.

24
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:16,085
We've also turned a few storerooms over to other purposes, like using them for

25
00:01:16,085 --> 00:01:16,520
meetings.

26
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:21,800
We try hard to involve members of the public in the theatre.

27
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:24,800
One way is by organising backstage tours,

28
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:30,800
so people can be shown round the building and learn how a theatre operates.

29
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:33,250
These are proving very popular.

30
00:01:33,250 --> 00:01:36,928
What we're finding is that people want to have lunch

31
00:01:36,928 --> 00:01:39,870
or a cup of coffee while they're here,

32
00:01:39,870 --> 00:01:44,820
so we're looking into the possibility of opening a cafe in due course.

33
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:46,740
We have a bookshop,

34
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:49,620
which specialises in books about drama,

35
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:52,500
and that attracts plenty of customers.

36
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:57,340
Then there are two large rooms that will be decorated next month,

37
00:01:57,340 --> 00:01:59,760
and they'll be available for hire,

38
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:03,420
for conferences and private functions, such as parties.

39
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:08,270
We're also considering hiring out costumes to amateur drama clubs.

40
00:02:08,270 --> 00:02:13,140
Now I want to tell you about our workshops.

41
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:18,400
We recently started a programme of workshops that anyone can join.

42
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:22,740
Eventually we intend to run courses in acting,

43
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:26,890
but we're waiting until we've got the right people in place as trainers.

44
00:02:26,890 --> 00:02:30,810
That's proving more difficult than we'd expected!

45
00:02:30,810 --> 00:02:35,841
There's a big demand to learn about the technical side of putting on a

46
00:02:35,841 --> 00:02:36,200
production,

47
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:41,000
and our lighting workshop has already started, with great success.

48
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,680
We've going to start one on sound next month.

49
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:48,663
A number of people have enquired about workshops on make-up,

50
00:02:48,663 --> 00:02:51,850
and that's something we're considering for the future.

51
00:02:51,850 --> 00:02:56,910
A surprise success is the workshop on making puppets

52
00:02:56,910 --> 00:03:00,894
we happen to have someone working here who does it as a hobby,

53
00:03:00,894 --> 00:03:03,040
and she offered to run a workshop.

54
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:07,080
It was so popular we've now running them every month!

55
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:13,000
Now, a word about the layout of the building.

56
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:19,500
The auditorium, stage and dressing rooms for the actors are all below ground level.

57
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:24,312
Here on the ground floor we have most of the rooms that the public

58
00:03:24,312 --> 00:03:25,000
doesn't see.

59
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,629
The majority are internal,

60
00:03:26,629 --> 00:03:30,700
so they have windows in the roof to light them.

61
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:37,360
Standing here in the foyer, you're probably wondering why the box office isn't here,

62
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:39,930
where the public would expect to find it.

63
00:03:39,930 --> 00:03:43,890
Well, you might have noticed it on your way in

64
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:49,009
although it's part of this building, it's next door with a separate entrance from

65
00:03:49,009 --> 00:03:49,740
the road.

66
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:54,540
For the theatre manager's office, you go across the foyer

67
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:56,940
and through the double doors,

68
00:03:56,940 --> 00:03:57,619
turn right,

69
00:03:57,619 --> 00:04:02,371
and it's the room at the end of the corridor, with the door on

70
00:04:02,371 --> 00:04:03,050
the left.

71
00:04:03,050 --> 00:04:08,133
The lighting box is where the computerised stage lighting is operated,

72
00:04:08,133 --> 00:04:11,830
and it's at the back of the building.

73
00:04:11,830 --> 00:04:18,375
When you're through the double doors, turn left, turn right at the water cooler

74
00:04:18,375 --> 00:04:21,180
and right again at the end.

75
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:24,600
It's the second room along that corridor.

76
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:28,440
The lighting box has a window into the auditorium,

77
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:31,000
which of course is below us.

78
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:36,310
The artistic director's office is through the double doors,

79
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:37,114
turn right,

80
00:04:37,114 --> 00:04:41,940
and it's the first room you come to on the right-hand side.

81
00:04:41,940 --> 00:04:48,059
And finally, for the moment, the room where I'll take you next 一 the

82
00:04:48,059 --> 00:04:49,000
relaxation room.

83
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:53,200
So if you'd like to come with me ...
